+# Local exact-platform fan-curve extension 0.13.1
+
+Base: BeardOverflow/msi-ec commit `d7fbbd88e6831e56801b860e46475cbf8ddbc7c1`.
+
+This local revision adds one `fan_curve` sysfs attribute only for:
+
+- Product: Raider 18 HX AI A2XWIG
+- Board: MS-1824
+- BIOS: E1824IMS.310
+- EC: 1824EMS1.108
+
+Format: 26 unsigned decimal bytes in this order:
+
+1. CPU temperature thresholds, 6 values
+2. CPU fan speed points, 7 values
+3. GPU temperature thresholds, 6 values
+4. GPU fan speed points, 7 values
+
+The driver itself establishes and verifies firmware fan mode `auto` plus Cooler Boost
+`on` before reading or writing curve bytes, and leaves that safe envelope active when it
+returns. It reads the whole original curve, validates the whole requested curve, writes
+all four regions, and reads everything back. On transaction or verification failure it
+first re-establishes the safe envelope, attempts every original byte even after a write
+error, and verifies the complete rollback. The captured factory curve is always accepted
+for rollback. Other curves must pass monotonicity, temperature, speed, and high-
+temperature floor constraints.
+
+The interface exposes no arbitrary EC address access. Debug mode remains disabled.
+Raw `ec_sys` write support remains disabled.
